Structure
Parent → Child

Step 1 — Parent Class
class Animal 
{
    void eat() 
    {
        System.out.println("Eating");
    }
}

Step 2 — Child Class
class Dog extends Animal
{
    void bark() 
    {
        System.out.println("Barking");
    }
}

Step 3 — Main Method
public class Main 
{
    public static void main(String[] args) 
    {
        Dog d = new Dog();
        d.eat();
        d.bark();
    }
}

Output
Eating
Barking
